  "implementation": [
    "At most two full readers; while busy, only a newer capture can start in the spare slot. Historical candidates stay queued.",
    "A completed reader seeds an independent cache and mutable OCR/page state. Native model sessions share weights; requests and outputs remain owned per thread. No second model initialization.",
    "Older readers cooperatively yield at OCR/stage boundaries while a newer sequence reads. Current processing finishes before historical continuation; failures release the waiting reader.",
    "GUI completion folds against the newest timeline and includes all in-flight and queued older sequences in compaction. Old completions do not replace the current page, HUD or gold reference.",
    "Pause, reset, mode change and close invalidate old results; one failure does not mark another worker idle. Visual/manual reads retain single-reader behavior."
  ],
